C3, REGISTERED: what each anchor implies for this tile's AI cap, and how
  the counter will score it. A ladder anchor is a B/(A+B) fit, so the
  study's 2 BM/(alpha b) reading is HIGH by (1 + phi + delta) (retraction
  (a), moe/bench/ai_model.py); alpha_a is unmeasured, so the corrected cap
  is a BRACKET over alpha_a in [0, 1] at delta = 0, the generous end.
  The counter's own alpha is a traffic slope with no level in it and is
  scored on 2 BM W / (b dR/dn) instead; see the C3 gate.
